alk", 139.34, 139.56], ["to", 139.56, 139.82], ["a", 139.82, 139.94], ["card.", 139.94, 140.26], ["Over", 140.52, 140.72], ["30", 140.72, 141.2], [",000", 141.2, 141.62], ["homes", 141.62, 142.0], ["are", 142.0, 142.26], ["already", 142.26, 142.76], ["pulling", 142.76, 143.06], ["them", 143.06, 143.28], ["out", 143.28, 143.5], ["of", 143.5, 143.6], ["their", 143.6, 143.74], ["beds", 143.74, 144.14], ["instead", 144.14, 144.56], ["of", 144.56, 144.74], ["washing", 144.74, 145.1], ["around", 145.1, 145.38], ["them.", 145.38, 145.78], ["Up", 145.98, 146.12], ["to", 146.12, 146.3], ["65", 146.3, 146.86], ["%", 146.86, 147.28], ["off", 147.28, 147.72], ["right", 147.72, 148.04], ["now.", 148.04, 148.42], ["With", 148.68, 148.86], ["a", 148.86, 148.98], ["90", 148.98, 149.28], ["-day", 149.28, 149.6], ["money", 149.6, 149.9], ["back", 149.9, 150.22], ["guarantee,", 150.22, 150.7], ["tap", 151.1, 151.26], ["below.", 151.26, 151.7]], "segments": [[0.0, 4.98, "Your doctor says nothing's wrong, your blood work is clean but you're still waking up blocked"], [4.98, 10.48, "every single morning. So here's what happens to your airways if you slide two capture cards"], [10.48, 15.46, "under your mattress and pillow and leave them there for four weeks. Okay, this is the part nobody's"], [15.46, 20.8, "talking about. Dust mites can directly damage your airway cells through mitochondrial injury"], [20.8, 26.32, "and abnormal autophagy. In plain English, the cells lining your airways can lose their"], [26.32, 31.7, "power and stop cleaning themselves up properly. So here's what happens to your airways if you"], [31.7, 36.8, "slide two capture cards under your mattress and pillow and leave them there for four weeks."], [37.14, 42.18, "Slide them in. That's the whole job. The first night while you sleep, the lure starts drawing"], [42.18, 47.5, "dust mites up out of the foam. The ones building up two inches under your face. That's the plant"], [47.5, 52.24, "derived pheromone lure, pulling them away from the place you breathe for eight hours a night."], [52.24, 57.5, "By the end of week one, most people find they're not reaching for a tissue the second they sit up."], [57.74, 63.78, "That's because every mite the lure pulls out stops dropping its 20 pellets a day of derpy one where"], [63.78, 68.76, "your face sleeps. The allergen that breaks down the junctions holding your airway lining together."], [69.22, 73.24, "Week two, you stop wondering if you're coming down with something and that clearer"], [73.24, 78.66, "by lunch feeling starts showing up at breakfast. That's the adhesive, locking every mite the"], [78.66, 84.54, "lure pulls in. So what it catches comes out of your bed instead of back into it. The craziest part?"], [84.82, 89.44, "You haven't sprayed a thing. You haven't stripped the bed. You haven't bought a new mattress."], [89.82, 95.56, "But every single night, the mattress you sleep on is giving them up. Week four, by now most"], [95.56, 100.48, "people are sleeping through more and waking up less blocked. Mornings start the way they did"], [100.48, 106.02, "years ago. And that background dread before you even open your eyes is finally gone. For"], [106.02, 111.86, "you and for whoever shares your bed. How is this possible? Most mite products try to kill them."], [112.08, 117.78, "But every dead one stays in the bed carrying the same allergen as a live one. This one pulls"], [117.78, 123.26, "them out alive. Dust mites have no eyes. They find each other by scent, a chemical signal."], [123.56, 128.06, "Capture cards mimic that signal. Drawing them up out of the foam and the adhesive"], [128.06, 133.44, "locks them on. It's lure and trap. The way pest control has caught things for decades"], [133.44, 140.26, "aimed at the one place nobody had. The inside of a mattress. Because a dead mite can't walk to a card."], [140.52, 145.78, "Over 30,000 homes are already pulling them out of their beds instead of washing around them."], [145.98, 151.7, "Up to 65% off right now. With a 90-day money back guarantee, tap below."]]}